Q: Change user input to lowercase A: <p>The Scanner is for getting input, not for translating or transforming it, and your code shouldn't even compile since you're calling a Scanner method that doesn't exist. You instead want to transform the String obtained.</p>
<p>You could simply do:</p>
<pre><code>String myLowerCaseInput = in.nextLine().toLowerCase();
</code></pre>
<p>As an aside, I highly doubt that you will want to create the Scanner object in this method, since you should only create <strong>one</strong> Scanner object based on <code>System.in</code>. If need be, pass that Scanner into this method using a parameter.</p>
<pre><code>protected String nextMove(Scanner in) {
    System.out.print(&quot;Please enter move: &quot;);
    return in.nextLine().toLowerCase();
}
</code></pre>
<p>or better...</p>
<pre><code>private static String nextMove(Scanner in) {
    String input = &quot;&quot;;
    do {
        System.out.print(&quot;Please enter move: &quot;);
        input = in.nextLine().trim().toLowerCase();
    } while (input.isEmpty() || input.length() != 1 || !&quot;abc&quot;.contains(input));
    return input;
}
</code></pre>
